# .github-guard — declarations github-guard reads (see the github-guard skill:
# https://github.com/antimatter-studios/agent-skills/blob/main/.claude/skills/github-guard/README.md).
# git-config format: check with `git config -f .github-guard --list`, and
# double-quote any value containing # or ;.

# Required status checks for main. A declaration beats discovery exactly.
#
# Discovery requires checks BY JOB NAME, which is a guess at the PR gate and
# drifts silently: a renamed job, an added workflow, or any future check
# reporting under the github-actions app changes what is required without
# anyone deciding to. Pinning it costs nothing and makes the intent reviewable.
#
# Written because the settings page had drifted. Before #101 the required
# contexts were exactly two -- `test-ubuntu-latest` and `validate against
# kernel squashfs driver` -- while the last run on main concluded three:
# `test-ubuntu-24.04-arm` had been passing all along and could not block a
# merge. Nothing compared the list against the jobs ci.yml defines, because
# the list did not live in the repository.
#
# `test-ubuntu-24.04-arm` is here for the failures it is the only leg that
# can see. `c_char` is unsigned on aarch64-linux and signed on x86_64, and
# this crate has a C ABI, so a `buf as *mut u8` that is a real cast on one
# target is a no-op cast on the other and clippy refuses it, and a `char`
# buffer written `[0i8; N]` does not compile on aarch64 at all. Both of those
# were sitting on main with no step that could see them (#78). rust-fs-ntfs#268
# is the same failure in the sibling driver, found by adding this exact leg.
# Advisory, it reports the breakage after the merge; required, it stops it.
# A cross `cargo check` would lint but not run, so the native runner stays.
#
# `validate against kernel squashfs driver` is the triple-agreement job: an
# image built by mksquashfs, read back by the in-kernel squashfs driver via a
# loop mount, by upstream unsquashfs, and by our own lssquashfs, across all
# five compressors. It is the only check that compares this reader against
# the kernel rather than against this repository's own expectations, and it
# runs on pull_request, so it gates.
#
# Deliberately NOT declared: the `test` job of release.yml. It triggers on a
# `v*.*.*` tag push and never on a pull request, and a required check that
# cannot report on a PR is a permanent block on every merge.
#
# Third-party reviewers are excluded before this file is read:
# github-protect-main.sh filters `select(.app.slug=="github-actions")` on
# every one of its queries. Verified against this repository -- the check
# suite of the most recent pull_request run contains exactly the three names
# below and nothing else.
#
# Names must match the check-run names GitHub reports. This workflow sets
# `name: test-${{ matrix.os }}` on the matrix job, so the runs are spelled
# `test-ubuntu-latest`, NOT the default `test / ubuntu-latest` job-matrix
# spelling other repositories in the constellation use.
[checks]
	required = test-ubuntu-latest
	required = test-ubuntu-24.04-arm
	required = "validate against kernel squashfs driver"
